<title>ITALY: Italy's Bologna sees November CPI at 3.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Bologna sees November CPI at 3.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BOLOGNA, Italy 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Bologna said its November consumer price index stood at 0.2 percent month-on-month and 3.5 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In October, Bologna's inflation rate was 0.2 and 3.9 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Bologna is one of 10 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.62 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to October 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.2  (0.2)	3.5 (3.9)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.2 (-0.3)	2.0 (2.4)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.2 (1.0)	 2.6 (2.5)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   1.0  (1.2)	7.2 (6.1)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.3  (0.0)	1.7 (2.9)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0 (1.3)	 4.9 (4.9)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.3 (-0.3)	2.6 (4.5)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.1 (0.1)	10.1 (10.2)</p>
<p>    Education			   1.5 (0.6)	 2.6 (2.0)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0 (0.0)	 2.7 (2.7)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0 (-0.2)	0.8 (1.1)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
